# Provider profile and qualification cache are machine-local run state, not
# evidence: the profile carries a credential reference and the cache is keyed
# by a subject digest that does not cover schema bytes, so committing it would
# invite a future run to reuse a verdict that no longer describes the contracts.
home/

# Battery outputs are transient WHILE A RUN IS IN FLIGHT. `deepreason qualify`
# writes qual-*.json only when it returns, so mid-run the file exists at zero
# bytes and committing it would enter an empty file into the record under a
# message calling it a result.
#
# These are real evidence once the run ENDS — including when it ends badly, as
# the 20B qual-after3.json did. Force-add them then:
#     git add -f experiments/live_gemma4_schema_2026-07-31/qual-*.json qual-*.err battery.log
qual-*.json
qual-*.err
battery.log
